                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "JAa19",
                  "name": "Notes body",
                  "fill": "$b:muted-foreground",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": 720,
                  "content": "Hierarchy by scale. A 64 px Discover title over a 4 px black rule, then Trending as the one dominant row: 5 larger posters (248 × 372) with rank numbers 1 to 5 in the data font.\nThe rows change shape by type. Popular and Netflix rows use 6 standard cards (200 × 300). Upcoming rows switch to 4 wide cards that lead with the date or year at 40 px, since the date matters most for something not out yet, and they carry no rating.\n\"In library\" becomes the system's black strong chip, so owned titles stand out across every row.\nServer: genres (Trending cards only) and the exact air date on upcoming TV (14 Oct and so on) are not in what the server sends today and need a server change. Title, type, year, poster, rating and library status are already sent. The rank is the position in the trending list.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$b:font-ui",
                  "fontSize": 13,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
