          "name": "Direction notes",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "fill": "$b:muted",
          "stroke": "$b:border",
          "strokeWidth": {
            "top": 1
          },
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 8,
          "padding": [
            28,
            40,
            40,
            40
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "dT7eZ",
              "name": "Notes heading",
              "fill": "$b:foreground",
              "content": "Direction notes · Delight",
              "fontFamily": "$b:font-ui",
              "fontSize": 15,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "ljuVv",
              "name": "Note 1",
              "fill": "$b:muted-foreground",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "Idea: the rows answer the owner's next question before he asks it. Each row says in one plain line where its titles come from; Trending is numbered because its order means something; In library is a solid black chip you can spot from across the row.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$b:font-ui",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "y3rJY",
              "name": "Note 2",
              "fill": "$b:muted-foreground",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "Upcoming TV turns dates into something you can read at a glance: a small date tab on the poster corner and an \"In 3 days\" countdown chip. Shows without a date say \"No date yet\", and a missing poster says \"No poster yet\" instead of leaving a grey box.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$b:font-ui",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "HkYR4",
              "name": "Note 3",
              "fill": "$b:muted-foreground",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "Static states drawn in place: Dune: Part Two (Trending, 2nd) shows pointer hover, with a soft lift and the one-line overview over the poster's lower half. Andor (Popular TV, 3rd) shows keyboard focus, a 2 px black ring with a 3 px gap.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$b:font-ui",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "azQoq",
              "name": "Note 4",
              "fill": "$b:muted-foreground",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "Server needs: overview is already sent. Genres need a server change. The date tab and countdown need the full premiere date for upcoming TV (today only the year is listed as sent). Countdowns are worked out in the browser from today's date. Trending rank is the order the server already returns.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$b:font-ui",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
